# KS-789 — Wednesday's task for Ornith, **DOCUMENTATION (`Blockchain/Dev/CONTRIBUTING.md`, no code)** (r2, rewritten 2026-09-16 20:15 after the r1 premise "There is no CI" was MEASURED FALSE; written from the file at develop M55 `48e65c435`: `Blockchain/Dev/CONTRIBUTING.md` read whole (680 lines by `wc -l`) with `### Pre-push preflight (KS-380) — run before every push` at `:360` read in full through `:408`, `### Adopted merge flow` `:445-481` and `### Review Requirements` `:596-609` read, every CI / Actions / workflow / status-check / review line in the file grepped and read; `Blockchain/Dev/docs/DEV-PROCESS.md` read for the `## Manual CI-gate equivalents` heading at `:77`). r1 is kept beside this file as `KS-789.md.pre-2010-cifact`. ⚠ NOT pre-measured in a clone: this commission is READ-ONLY against the Secuura checkout — every `-` line was measured byte-for-byte at the tip, and the replacement was applied in memory to the tip text to prove the three Required tokens go absent → present inside the section (see the raise notes).

## What to change (one paragraph)

`CONTRIBUTING.md:384-386` justifies TWO mechanisms — the pre-push hook's graceful degradation, and its
documented `--no-verify` bypass — with a single clause: **"CI is the hard gate."** It is not: **no status
check is required to merge into `develop`** (measured 2026-09-16 through the GitHub rules API), so a red
or missing workflow run blocks nothing. The passage therefore tells every reader that a leg which
degraded, or a push that used the bypass, will be *stopped* later by CI — and CI stops nothing. The
sentence is **load-bearing for a decision an author makes under pressure**, because how sparingly you
reach for `--no-verify` depends on what is standing behind you. The replacement states what does stand
behind it — the merge rule this same file already defines (a PR merges only once TESTED, step 6 of
*Adopted merge flow*, and its Test Evidence block says what ran) — the obligation that follows (a bypassed
push says so in that block, naming which legs ran), and a pointer to `docs/DEV-PROCESS.md` §*Manual
CI-gate equivalents*. **Removing the bypass is explicitly NOT proposed** — the ticket is clear that a hook
that cannot be bypassed makes the repository unpushable (KS-788). The replacement deliberately says
nothing about whether GitHub Actions is running or retired — see the raise notes.

