## Premises (measured)

Every factual claim the eleven `+` lines assert or rely on, with the instrument that measured it on
2026-09-16 (~20:07–20:15). GitHub calls are read-only REST GETs on `Secuura/Distributed_Secuura`.

1. **"no status check is required to merge into `develop`"** —
   `GET /repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/rules/branches/develop` → HTTP 200, exactly three rules, all from
   ruleset 18499832 `require-pr-gates` (enforcement `active`, targets `refs/heads/develop` +
   `refs/heads/main`, updated 2026-09-10T09:23+10:00): `deletion`, `non_fast_forward`, `pull_request`
   (`required_approving_review_count: 0`). **No `required_status_checks` rule.** Corroborated by
   `GET /branches/develop` → `protected: true`, `protection.required_status_checks.enforcement_level: "off"`,
   `contexts: []`, `checks: []`. `GET /branches/develop/protection` → **HTTP 403** `"Resource not accessible
   by personal access token"` (classic protection not readable with this PAT; the rules endpoint is the
   instrument that answered).
2. **"a red or missing workflow run blocks nothing"** — follows from 1. Runs exist and are mostly red:
   `GET /actions/runs?event=pull_request&per_page=30` (2026-09-14T15:36Z → 2026-09-15T11:09Z) → 16 `failure`,
   12 `success`, 2 `cancelled`; `pr` 5/5 failure, `PR Security Gates (KS-168)` 5/5 failure, `Security
   Scanning` 5/5 failure. "Missing" is kept because runs were 100% `startup_failure` through 2026-09-07
   (ticket comment 2026-09-07; `GET /actions/runs?created=2026-09-07..2026-09-09` still 47/100
   `startup_failure`) — the sentence stays true in either state.
3. **"a PR merges only once TESTED (step 6 of *Adopted merge flow*, below)"** —
   `git show 48e65c435:Blockchain/Dev/CONTRIBUTING.md`: `:445` heading `### Adopted merge flow (Kam,
   2026-08-25) — the standing flow` (below `:385`); `:466` `6. **The author merges once the PR is TESTED —
   not the reviewer.**`; `:480` `**Untested, or no GO → no merge.**`; `:598` repeats it in *Review
   Requirements*.
4. **"its Test Evidence block says what actually ran"** — same file, `:547` `A line must say what
   happened, not what applies. "Run and passing" means a run` and `:461-462` (results go in the PR
   description's Test Evidence block).
5. **"The local runs that fill that block are listed in `docs/DEV-PROCESS.md` § *Manual CI-gate
   equivalents*"** — `git show 48e65c435:Blockchain/Dev/docs/DEV-PROCESS.md`: `:77` `## Manual CI-gate
   equivalents`, `:79` "Every job that used to gate a PR, and the local command that now stands in for
   it"; CONTRIBUTING.md `:538-540` "They run locally. The command, pass criterion and wall-clock for each
   … are in `docs/DEV-PROCESS.md` under *Manual CI-gate equivalents*." The link target path
   `docs/DEV-PROCESS.md` exists relative to `Blockchain/Dev/` (`git show` succeeded).
6. **"A bypassed push must say so in the PR's Test Evidence block, naming which legs did and did not
   run"** — this is the change, not a fact: it is the ticket's fix-shape item 2 (Linear KS-789 description,
   read 20:07). It applies the file's own standing rule at `:547-550` (a Test Evidence line says what
   happened) to the bypass case, and the verdict it asks authors to quote is real: `preflight.sh:704-733`
   at the tip prints `N/15 legs ran` and names SKIPPED legs. **Not a Kam ruling** — flagged for review.
7. **"never blocks a push"** (kept from `:385`) — unchanged text; `preflight.sh:708-753` exits 0 on
   SKIPPED legs unless `PREFLIGHT_STRICT_LEGS=1` (default off, `:129`, `:749`).

8. **Measured but deliberately NOT written into the doc — does CI run the shell suites?** (Wednesday's
   20:25 correction asked for step names, not workflow names.) `GET
   /actions/workflows/{pr-security-gates.yml,security-scan.yml,pr-platform-suites.yml}/runs?created=2026-09-02..2026-09-16`
   → 539 runs; `GET /actions/runs/{id}/jobs` for each, steps matched on "shell test suites": the
   `pr-security-gates.yml` job `Code Security Gates` step `All shell test suites (KS-666 / KS-731 — globbed,
   not listed)` EXECUTED in 200 runs between 2026-09-10T11:49Z and 2026-09-15T14:22Z (pull_request 111
   failure + 4 success; push 79 failure + 6 success); no `security-scan.yml` or `pr-platform-suites.yml`
   run executed a shell-suite step. Job log for run 34961722314 (`GET /actions/jobs/104356628320/logs`,
   HTTP 200, 97 KB): the runner printed 35 `=== <suite> ===` headers and `shell suites: 33 passed, 2
   failed (of 35)` (FAILED: `ks949_main_seed_idempotence.test.sh`, `systemTest/__tests__/manifest_readers_agree.test.sh`).
   So **CI does run the shell suites on PRs and develop pushes since 2026-09-10, and the step is red**;
   `preflight.sh:548-550` ("BOTH … workflow steps are dormant", measured at e26cfce2b) is stale in present
   tense. None of this is needed by the `+` lines, which claim only item 1.

Claims deliberately NOT made (unmeasurable or contested): that Actions is retired; that Actions runs on
every PR; that a reviewer re-checks legs; anything about `main`.

## Notes for the raise (not for the model)

- **Why r2 exists.** r1 said "There is no CI. GitHub Actions is retired for this repository", taken from
  the ticket (2026-09-04) and its 2026-09-07 comment (2,000 runs 100% `startup_failure`). Wednesday
  measured it FALSE at 20:05; re-measured for this rewrite: `GET /actions/workflows` → 23 workflows, all
  `active`; `GET /actions/runs?created=<range>` (first 100 per range) → 2026-09-07..09 47/100
  `startup_failure`, then **zero** `startup_failure` in 09-10..11, 09-12..13 and 09-14..16 — Actions
  resumed starting jobs between 2026-09-09 and 2026-09-10. PR runs execute for real (`pr` 799–1112 s each;
  run 34961722314 `PR Security Gates` executed step `All shell test suites (KS-666 / KS-731 — globbed, not
  listed)` → `failure`). The 09:53 KS-910 card text "CI runs the suites" is Wednesday's option label that
  Kam tapped, NOT an independent observation, and is not used as evidence here (correction 20:25). `GET
  /actions/runs?branch=develop&event=push&per_page=30` → newest 2026-09-15T14:22Z; 24 failure, 6
  cancelled, 0 success. r1 also named "the reviewer" as the backstop; under the standing flow (`:466-478`,
  Kam 2026-09-11) the sign-off is the QA gate verdict at head + Wednesday's GO, so r2 points at the merge
  rule instead of a reviewer.
- **Self-consistency of the file after this edit — grepped, every CI / Actions / workflow / status-check
  line.** The file is ALREADY internally inconsistent about CI, before this edit:
  - says Actions/checks RUN or GATE (present tense): `:87-89` (pre-merge gate green on the merge commit;
    "the CI gate stack"), `:93-105` (KS-380 required checks report on `hotfix/*` → `main` PRs; a
    platform hotfix "stays BLOCKED"), `:187` ("CI fails when the committed catalog is stale"), `:191` ("a CI
    staleness gate"), `:436-438` ("Until that box is ticked the checks run but don't block").
  - says Actions is RETIRED / nothing runs: `:419-423` ("None of the checks listed here runs any more"),
    `:449-450` ("permanently, now that GitHub Actions is retired (Kam, 2026-08-27)"), `:485-486` ("With
    Actions retired no check runs at all"), `:494-504` (the retirement section), `:539-545` ("every retired
    CI job"; "with Actions retired it cannot report anyway"), `:603-604` ("GitHub Actions is retired … there
    are no CI checks to pass").
  **The replacement adds no new contradiction:** it asserts only that no check is *required* on `develop`
  (true under both readings, and agreeing with `:436-438` and `:506-510` "must not be enabled") and points
  at the merge rule `:466-480` already states. It does NOT reconcile the two groups above. **After the
  measurement, the "retired" group is stale in present tense** (Actions has started jobs daily since
  2026-09-10), and `:93-100`'s "required checks … stays BLOCKED" is stale for `develop` (no required
  check). **Reconciling them — is Kam's 2026-08-27 retirement ruling superseded now that jobs run again,
  and should the docs say CI runs-but-does-not-gate? — is Kam's decision, not the model's and not this
  ticket's.** Raise it alongside this PR.
- **Same false clause in a second file, out of scope here.** The ticket's 2026-09-07 comment found
